The host genome plays a critical role in defining an individual’s clinical phenotype and susceptibility to asthma exacerbations
 \cite{RuanShi2020}
 \cite{ZhangZhang2018}. Understanding these specific single-nucleotide polymorphisms provides novel insights into disease pathology and therapeutic responses, highlighting the importance of developing genotype-guided, personalized treatment strategies to mitigate the severe global burden of asthma exacerbations
 \cite{PlichtaPanek2025}
.
