Conclusion
The host genome exerts distinct age-dependent influences on the clinical presentation of asthma
 \cite{BaekJung2022}
. Childhood-onset asthma is a highly heritable, systemic disorder driven by epithelial and skin barrier impairment (FLG, GSDMB/ORMDL3) and Th2-mediated allergic inflammation
 \cite{PividoriSchoettler2018}
. Adult-onset asthma is less heritable, more lung-centered, and driven by immune-mediated progression pathways (predominantly in the HLA region) interacting with cumulative environmental exposures
 \cite{BaekJung2022}
.
These findings emphasize that clinical trials and genomic risk stratification models must account for age of onset to achieve the therapeutic precision required for personalized asthma management
 \cite{ShiZhang2022}
.
