B. Polymorphisms in Airway Responsiveness or Remodeling Genes
Unlike inflammatory genes, remodeling and responsiveness genes directly affect the physical properties of the airway wall, smooth muscle contractility, or physical barrier integrity:
GSDMB (rs7216389, rs2305480) (Question 29): The chromosome 17q12-21 region is the most robustly replicated childhood asthma locus
 \cite{LiChristenson2021}
. The intronic variant rs7216389 acts as a powerful eQTL regulating GSDMB expression in bronchial epithelial cells
 \cite{LiChristenson2021}
. In prospective cohort studies, children carrying the homozygous TT genotype of rs7216389 exhibited a 2.66-fold increased hazard of early-childhood exacerbations (95\\\\% CI: 1.58–4.48; P=0.0002) that persisted from ages 1 through 6
 \cite{ParkTantisira2017}
. The coding missense variant rs2305480 (G allele) is likewise significantly associated with severe asthma (OR = 1.27) and longitudinal exacerbation frequency (P=0.0086)
 \cite{LiChristenson2021}
. (No specific exacerbation data are provided for rs4794820).
CTNNA3 (rs7915695) (Question 30): This gene encodes alpha-T-catenin, an essential component of the cell-adherence junction complex in epithelial cells and airway smooth muscle
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
. The intronic SNP rs7915695 met genome-wide significance in pediatric trials (P=2.19×10 
−8
 ), with risk-allele carriers experiencing a mean of 6.05 exacerbations compared to 3.71 for homozygous reference carriers
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
. Lower CTNNA3 expression disrupts cell-to-cell adhesion, predisposing the airway to mechanical instability and hyperresponsiveness during exacerbations
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
. (No specific data are provided for rs7923078 or rs6480203).
SEMA3D (rs993312) (Question 32): Semaphorin 3D regulates endothelial cell migration, angiogenesis, and immune cell recruitment
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
. The intronic variant rs993312 regulates SEMA3D expression, which is significantly increased in bronchoalveolar lavage samples and airway smooth muscle cells from asthmatic patients compared to controls
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
. It is strongly associated with severe asthma exacerbation risk, particularly in African Americans, where risk-allele carriers experience more than double the rate of severe, recurrent attacks (3.91 vs. 1.53 in BioVU; 6.0 vs. 3.25 in CAMP)
 \cite{McGeachieWu2015}
.
4. Glucocorticoid Receptor Pathway Loci (NR3C1) (Questions 11, 24)
Because inhaled corticosteroids (ICS) represent the primary anti-inflammatory maintenance therapy in asthma, polymorphisms in the glucocorticoid receptor gene (NR3C1) directly affect exacerbation susceptibility by modulating steroid sensitivity
 \cite{MartnezAguilarRoNavarro2014}
:
rs41423247 (BclI): The rs41423247 polymorphism is associated with altered glucocorticoid sensitivity
 \cite{KeskinUluca2016}
. In acute rescue settings, pediatric patients presenting with acute moderate-to-severe asthma exacerbations who are homozygous for the G allele (GG genotype) show a significantly better clinical response, characterized by rapid, significant improvement in FEV 
1
​
