Ancestry-Specific Genomic Architecture: Minor allele frequencies (MAFs) and linkage disequilibrium (LD) block patterns vary profoundly across different ancestries, meaning that European-descent "tag" SNPs frequently fail to capture the true causative variants in populations of African, Latino, or Asian descent
