Systematic Review of the Association of TNF-α Promoter Polymorphisms (rs1800629 and rs1800630) with Asthma Severity and Exacerbation Frequency
To the Editorial Board of the Journal of Asthma:
1. Pathophysiological and Molecular Rationale
Tumor Necrosis Factor-alpha (TNF-α) is a key pro-inflammatory cytokine encoded by the TNFA gene on chromosome 6p21
 \cite{AlAhmadAli2025}
 \cite{XuLi2017}. As a pleiotropic mediator, TNF-α plays a fundamental role in orchestrating both innate and adaptive immune responses in the respiratory mucosa
 \cite{AlAhmadAli2025}
