Conversely, the neighboring rs1800630 (-863C/A) variant acts as a major regulator of IgE synthesis and general atopic susceptibility, but lacks direct, independent validation as a standalone predictor of longitudinal exacerbation frequency. Future multi-ethnic, prospective trials incorporating dense MHC haplotyping and objective environmental exposure metrics are required to definitively establish the clinical biomarker utility of these promoter loci.
