Elevated IgE and Fibrosis: Clinically, the T allele of rs1800469 is significantly associated with elevated total immunoglobulin E (IgE) levels and an increased risk of progressive bronchial remodeling
 \cite{PlichtaPanek2025}
. This allele has also been found to negatively correlate with baseline spirometric values, directly predisposing patients to progressive airflow limitation
 \cite{KowinJonakowski2025}.
Asthma Severity and Control: In systematic meta-analyses of diverse pediatric and adult cohorts, the -509T variant has been identified as the TGFB1 polymorphism with the strongest association to overall asthma severity
 \cite{PlichtaPanek2025}
